    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by the elite speed-category utility of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13). Facing the lefty Rogers, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an optimized situational profile; his score is significantly inflated by an advantageous park factor and a slow pitcher delivery window, which maximizes his stolen base potential\u2014the primary needle-mover for our Roto standings. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (73.89) and **Kyle Schwarber** (70.57) provide formidable top-of-order stability against Singer. Despite the marginal platoon downgrade for **Trea Turner**, his matchup against a mid-tier xERA pitcher (4.51) coupled with his leadoff spot ensures elite volume for runs scored.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the volume of our fringe starters against the limited efficiency of **Lars Nootbaar** (43.93) and **Chase Meidroth** (44.88). While **Chase Meidroth** is projected for a suboptimal matchup against Sandoval\u2019s elite 2.08 xERA, his leadoff placement provided just enough buffer to keep him in the lineup over bench options like **Colt Keith** or **Nelson Velazquez**. **Lars Nootbaar** remains in the lineup purely due to the dynamic platoon edge, though his sub-45 score puts him on the bubble; he remains a candidate for an early pull if his first two at-bats reflect the SP skill deficit. We continue to monitor the status of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Christian Yelich**, who are unavailable today, leaving us to rely on **Carson Benge** (54.02) to bridge the gap in the outfield. \n\nLooking at the slate, the matchup for **Junior Caminero** (63.19) is a highlight; despite the tough park factor, his high xwOBA (0.370) against Blackburn keeps him as a strong start. Conversely, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Chase Meidroth**; the matchup against an elite lefty is our primary risk factor today. Ensure that **Luke Raley** (55.33) is monitored for any 